  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Ownership and data flow",
      "items": [
        "App owns every Entity; handles are Rc-like, so parents hold strong Entity<T> and back-pointers are WeakEntity",
        "Data flows down by read/update; intent flows up by cx.emit + subscribe, never a strong parent handle",
        "notify/observe means re-read me; emit/subscribe carries a typed event; dropping a Subscription cancels it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Layers",
      "items": [
        "Domain crates: pure rules, no gpui, no I/O, plain unit tests",
        "Model Entities: app state and stores in a crate with no UI dependency (Zed: project, terminal, git)",
        "View Entities: impl Render and own UI state (Zed: project_panel, terminal_view, git_ui)",
        "Window root: Zed's Workspace or gpui-component's Root, the first view in the window"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Async and persistence",
      "items": [
        "Commands stay synchronous; I/O goes behind a port trait with a real and a fake adapter",
        "Model spawns work on the background executor and keeps the Task: drop cancels it",
        "Results come back through the WeakEntity the spawn hands over; async contexts are fallible"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Keyboard, settings and theme",
      "items": [
        "Every intent is an action, handled by on_action inside a key_context; keymaps are JSON data loaded by bind_keys",
        "Focus (FocusHandle, Focusable) picks the dispatch path, so one key can mean different things per context",
        "Settings and theme are Globals read everywhere and watched with observe_global; each crate registers its own in init(cx)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Testing seams",
      "items": [
        "Pure crates: plain #[test], no gpui linked",
        "Models: #[gpui::test] with TestAppContext and fake adapters behind a test-support feature",
        "Views: VisualTestContext simulate_keystrokes / simulate_click / run_until_parked, no window or GPU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Sources (primary)",
      "items": [
        "Ideal design, not Personal Ledger's code; claims and reasons in docs/research/gpui-desktop-architecture.md",
        "gpui at tag gpui-v0.2.2: github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/gpui-v0.2.2/crates/gpui",
        "Zed workspace at 28d0a35: github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/28d0a3547f16b9609b301b48ab363bfca649c864/crates",
        "gpui-component v0.5.1: github.com/longbridge/gpui-component/tree/v0.5.1/crates/ui",
        "Nathan Sobo, Ownership and data flow in GPUI: zed.dev/blog/gpui-ownership"
      ]
    }
  ]
